##sequence-region NC_001133.9 1 230218
##species https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/Taxonomy/Browser/wwwtax.cgi?id=559292
#
# A hand-assembled excerpt of GCF_000146045.2_R64_genomic.gff: 14 gene units chosen to cover
# the shapes a loader has to survive, in NCBI annotwriter's own column layout, directive set
# and attribute spelling.
#
# EVERY LOCUS HERE IS REAL, at its real coordinates, strand and gene_biotype. The three the
# coordinate round-trip is asserted against -- BDH1, ECM31, GPD1 -- are among the 36 rows the
# atlas held before any GFF3 was parsed, so they are an independent check on the 1-based
# inclusive -> 0-based half-open conversion rather than a copy of this parser's own output.
# An earlier draft of this file invented spans and gave Q0140 to a tRNA (Q0140 is VAR1); a
# fixture that puts a real accession on the wrong gene is a trap for whoever reads it next.
#
# Deliberately illustrative rather than checked: the partial=true/start_range/end_range on
# YAL068C, the gene_synonym lists, and every protein_id/transcript_id accession. Nothing
# asserts on those, and they are here so the file parses like the real one. YAR061W's exon
# also carries no product=, which the real file does supply -- kept that way on purpose, so
# a gene whose annotation states no product at all has a case here.
#
# Coverage: minus strand (YAL068C, SNR161); mitochondrial (tP(UGG)Q, COX1, VAR1, 21S rRNA on
# NC_001224.1); tRNA; pseudogene, as RefSeq writes it -- feature TYPE `pseudogene`, not
# `gene`; an escaped comma in a product (BDH1's real '(R,R)-butanediol dehydrogenase');
# multi-exon (EFB1 2 exons, COX1 3); Name != locus_tag (PAU8/YAL068C, COX1/Q0045,
# VAR1/Q0140, TRN1/YNCA0002W); loci with no gene= at all, whose standard_name is therefore
# NULL (YAL067W-A, tP(UGG)Q, YAR061W); and SNR18, which really does sit inside the EFB1
# intron and so exercises the nested-gene path.
